// Our previous theorem shows the entire C encrypt function is equiavalent to
// the Cryptol encrypt function with the "reverse key" caveat. We can leverage
// all of that work in this proof by now treating the entire encrypt function
// as equiavalent and uninterpreting it. Then, the solver is just making sure
// that we actually reverse the key correctly, and allocate enough space for
// the expanded key.
encryptR_theorem <- llvm_verify CSpeck "encryptR" [encrypt_theorem] true encryptR_setup (unint_z3 ["encrypt"]);